  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds read and write in bzip2recover when a\n     .bz2 file yields more than BZ_MAX_HANDLED_BLOCKS block boundaries\n     (ELSCVE-178967)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-42250.patch: correct the off-by-one in the\n       block-count guard in bzip2recover.c, so the scanning loop stops one\n       block earlier instead of indexing one past bStart, bEnd, rbStart\n       and rbEnd.\n     - CVE-2026-42250",
